cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Kanchi TEI: a demonstration edition pipeline for South Indian temple legends"
message: >-
  If you refer to this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
  Most of the apparatus machinery in this repository is still demonstration
  scaffolding rather than a peer-reviewed critical edition; see each text's
  own sourceDesc and notesStmt for what is and is not a verified
  transcription before citing any specific reading.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ani
    family-names: Chandrashekhar
repository-code: "https://github.com/Achndrs4/Kanchi-Portfolio"
abstract: >-
  A working demonstration of a digital scholarly edition pipeline: TEI P5
  sources with a parallel-segmentation critical apparatus, a schema generated
  from a TEI ODD, an eXist-db application publishing the corpus over RESTXQ,
  XSLT transformations to HTML and CIDOC-CRM RDF, and a Python service for
  Devanagari and Tamil script conversion.
keywords:
  - digital humanities
  - TEI
  - XML
  - eXist-db
  - XQuery
  - XSLT
  - Linked Open Data
  - CIDOC-CRM
  - Sanskrit
  - Tamil
  - critical edition
license: MIT
version: 0.1.6
date-released: "2026-09-20"
